{
 "_readme": [
  "Which menu items the library shows, and in what order.",
  "",
  "Read by dge/js/menu.js at boot. If this file is missing or malformed, the menus",
  "stay exactly as written in dge/index.html — nothing disappears because a config",
  "file broke.",
  "",
  "Set enabled:false to hide an item. Reorder the arrays to reorder the menu. Items",
  "listed here but absent from the page are ignored; items on the page but absent",
  "from these arrays are left alone in place, so adding a new button to the markup",
  "does not require touching this file first.",
  "",
  "  requires   who sees an item. 'all' (default), 'admin' (either tier), or",
  "             'superadmin'. This is a tidiness gate, not access control — see",
  "             keys.json for what that means.",
  "  feature    only show when this is switched on. Currently only 'auth', which",
  "             follows AUTH_CONFIG.enabled in dge/js/config.js.",
  "  action     a function on window, called on click.",
  "  href       a URL, navigated to on click. Relative to dge/.",
  "",
  "NOT HERE, ON PURPOSE — one source of truth each:",
  "  reading scripts      SCRIPT_OPTIONS in dge/js/config.js",
  "  feature switches     FEATURE_FLAGS in dge/js/config.js",
  "  passkeys             admin/config/keys.json",
  "  the landing page     admin/config/landing.json",
  "  everything else      admin/config/config-overrides.json",
  "",
  "The 'commentary' topBar entry was removed 10 Sep 2026 with the button itself: the commentary bar above the verses (render.js dgeRenderCommentaryBar) carries every name and switch, so the global 💬 icon was the same control in a worse place. #commentaryPopup still exists for a verse card's '+N 💬' overflow tab."
 ],
